      {
        "id": 86454,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-12T04:06:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It goes by instances of damage, not points.&nbsp; This matters for those effects that hit everything twice, such as Char, Explosives Wagon, Cursed Acolyte, and \"Diplomatic Envoy\".&nbsp; In all cases, if you have a Decoy Projection or Stealth Bot out and one of these effects hits all hero targets, you can first choose to resolve the damage against one of the heroes.&nbsp; You redirect the first instance to Decoybot, and if they're still alive, you then redirect the second instance.&nbsp; You then move on to the next hero.&nbsp; If enough damage reduction is in play, you might manage to have the Decoybot still be around after each hero character card has been damaged - in which case Decoybot <em>itself</em> is also directly targeted by the blast because it's a hero target.</p><p>For example, Char is in play and there are no bonuses to damage; Stealth Bot has 5 HP and it innately reduces all damage it takes by 1.&nbsp; Char hits Unity for 2 fire and 2 toxic, which becomes 1 and 1 to Stealthy.&nbsp; Then another hero takes 2 and 2, which becomes 1 and 1 to the bot.&nbsp; Then a third hero takes 2 fire, which becomes 1 fire to Stealth Bot, killing it, and then that hero must take the 2 toxic.</p><p>Example 2:&nbsp; All other heroes besides Unity are incapped.&nbsp; Char hits Unity for 2 and 2, which becomes 1 and 1 to Stealth Bot.&nbsp; Char then hits Stealth Bot for 2 and 2 which becomes 1 and 1.&nbsp; Assuming Stealth Bot was at full, she survives, but if even one hero was alive and redirected damage to her, she wouldn't.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:10:27.099Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
