        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>It goes by instances of damage, not points.&nbsp; This matters for those effects that hit everything twice, such as Char, Explosives Wagon, Cursed Acolyte, and &quot;Diplomatic Envoy&quot;.&nbsp; In all cases, if you have a Decoy Projection or Stealth Bot out and one of these effects hits all hero targets, you can first choose to resolve the damage against one of the heroes.&nbsp; You redirect the first instance to Decoybot, and if they&#39;re still alive, you then redirect the second instance.&nbsp; You then move on to the next hero.&nbsp; If enough damage reduction is in play, you might manage to have the Decoybot still be around after each hero character card has been damaged - in which case Decoybot <em>itself</em> is also directly targeted by the blast because it&#39;s a hero target.</p><p>For example, Char is in play and there are no bonuses to damage; Stealth Bot has 5 HP and it innately reduces all damage it takes by 1.&nbsp; Char hits Unity for 2 fire and 2 toxic, which becomes 1 and 1 to Stealthy.&nbsp; Then another hero takes 2 and 2, which becomes 1 and 1 to the bot.&nbsp; Then a third hero takes 2 fire, which becomes 1 fire to Stealth Bot, killing it, and then that hero must take the 2 toxic.</p><p>Example 2:&nbsp; All other heroes besides Unity are incapped.&nbsp; Char hits Unity for 2 and 2, which becomes 1 and 1 to Stealth Bot.&nbsp; Char then hits Stealth Bot for 2 and 2 which becomes 1 and 1.&nbsp; Assuming Stealth Bot was at full, she survives, but if even one hero was alive and redirected damage to her, she wouldn&#39;t.</p>",
